Here's how to handle each scenario in MSTest:

## 1. Windows-only tests (platform filtering)

```csharp
[TestMethod]
[TestCategory("WindowsOnly")]
[System.Runtime.Versioning.SupportedOSPlatform("windows")]
public void RegistryTest()
{
    if (!OperatingSystem.IsWindows())
        Assert.Inconclusive("Requires Windows");

    // Registry access code here
}
```

Or use a condition attribute with a helper:

```csharp
[TestMethod]
[DoNotParallelize] // if registry access isn't thread-safe
public void RegistryTest()
{
    Assert.IsTrue(OperatingSystem.IsWindows(), "This test requires Windows.");
    // ...
}
```

## 2. Skip in CI (environment-based skip)

```csharp
[TestMethod]
[TestCategory("RequiresGPU")]
public void GpuTest()
{
    if (Environment.GetEnvironmentVariable("CI") is not null)
        Assert.Inconclusive("Skipped in CI — requires local GPU");

    // GPU test logic
}
```

Filter at the runner level in CI:

```bash
dotnet test --filter "TestCategory!=RequiresGPU"
```

## 3. Flaky external API (retry pattern)

MSTest doesn't have a built-in retry, but you can use `[DataRow]` tricks or a custom attribute. The simplest pattern:

```csharp
[TestMethod]
[TestCategory("Flaky")]
public void WeatherApiTest()
{
    const int maxRetries = 3;
    Exception? last = null;

    for (int i = 0; i < maxRetries; i++)
    {
        try
        {
            // Call weather API and assert
            return; // success
        }
        catch (Exception ex)
        {
            last = ex;
            Thread.Sleep(1000 * (i + 1)); // backoff
        }
    }

    Assert.Fail($"Failed after {maxRetries} retries: {last?.Message}");
}
```

Or with MSTest 3.x+, use the built-in retry:

```csharp
[TestMethod]
[Retry(3)] // MSTest 3.x+
public void WeatherApiTest()
{
    // Flaky API call + assertions
}
```

## 4. Cleanup even on failure (use `[TestCleanup]` or `try/finally`)

```csharp
[TestClass]
public class TempFileTests
{
    private string? _tempFile;

    [TestInitialize]
    public void Setup()
    {
        _tempFile = Path.GetTempFileName();
    }

    [TestCleanup]
    public void Cleanup()
    {
        if (_tempFile is not null && File.Exists(_tempFile))
            File.Delete(_tempFile);
    }

    [TestMethod]
    public void ProcessTempFile()
    {
        File.WriteAllText(_tempFile!, "test data");
        // Assertions — cleanup runs even if this throws
    }
}
```

`[TestCleanup]` is guaranteed to run regardless of test outcome, similar to a `finally` block.

---

**Summary table:**

| Scenario | Approach |
|----------|----------|
| Platform gate | `OperatingSystem.IsWindows()` + `Assert.Inconclusive` |
| Skip in CI | Env var check or `--filter TestCategory!=X` |
| Flaky test | `[Retry(3)]` (MSTest 3.x) or manual loop |
| Cleanup | `[TestCleanup]` method on the test class |
